import LOEIS.A063.A063405.Defs

set_option linter.unusedVariables false

/-!
# A063405

T(n,m) for positive n,m is the first integer we get when iterating f starting with f(n/m), where function f on rationals is defined as f(p/q)=abs(p-q)/NextOddCollatz(p)(we assume p,q coprime), where NextOddCollatz(p) is the next odd number that is found in the Collatz trajectory of p. When no integer is reached by iteration, T(n,m)=0.

The 101 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A063405

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `1`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
  [0, 1, 0, 3, 4, 0, 3, 1, 1, 0,
    4, 3, 2, 1, 0, 2, 3, 1, 4, 2,
    0, 2, 6, 7, 3, 9, 10, 0, 7, 3,
    5, 1, 3, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 3, 2,
    3, 4, 5, 6, 0, 3, 4, 9, 3, 1,
    2, 3, 1, 4, 0, 9, 1, 9, 4, 9,
    12, 13, 5, 15, 16, 0, 9, 2, 3, 3,
    7, 1, 2, 4, 1, 2, 2, 0, 7, 9,
    2, 3, 3, 9, 2, 1, 1, 3, 3, 4,
